    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Doggy Wash Express is a self-service dog washing station set up on avenue de Saint-Barthélemy, in the north of Nice. It's a small company (SAS) created in late October 2024, with its registered office in Nice; several business directories and the company's own page place the washing booth at this address on avenue Saint-Barthélemy.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The concept is self-service dog washing, no appointment needed: an equipped tub takes dogs of all sizes, with shampoo, conditioner, anti-parasite treatment and drying, for a supervised wash in just a few minutes. According to the sources found online, the station would be accessible 7 days a week from 8am to 8pm, and payment is card-only via a terminal. <strong>The exact price could not be confirmed with certainty</strong> and the exact postcode (06000 or 06100 depending on the source) remains to be confirmed — it's best to check these details directly on site or via the business's Facebook/Instagram page before going.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: before heading over, a quick call or a message on the business's social media confirms that the booth is actually working and that the advertised price hasn't changed — this is still a young concept, with few reviews online so far.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Avenue Saint-Barthélemy serves the north of Nice, between the station area and the hills leading up to Saint-Pierre-de-Féric — handy for a quick wash before or after a walk in the Nice hills.</p>
